;; The binary IR (queue 329): the code objects of a module compiled ahead as arbace.python.aot writes them into its
;; package (ir-binary), read at import in place of the printed IR's text (load.go), so a compiled program's import
;; parses no EDN. The same code objects as ReadIR makes from the text, in the same order (the interned names, the
;; codes' creation events): a module whose IR has a shape the writer does not know keeps its text.
;;
;; The layout: irBinMagic; the strings, a count then each one's byte length and bytes; then the module's code object.
;; A count, an index into the strings or a length is an unsigned varint (encoding/binary's), an integer a zigzag varint.
;; A code object: name, qualname and kind (string indices: kind the keyword's name, "" when absent); its flags (a count,
;; the keywords' names); argcount, posonly, kwonly; locals, cells, frees and names (a count, the names); its docstring
;; (0 none, 1 a string, 2 a value loaded as a constant); its constants (a count, each a constant); threaded (a count,
;; the integers); its instructions (a count, each its operation's name and its argument); its handlers (a count, each
;; four integers and lasti, 0 or 1); firstlineno; its warnings (a count, each a message and four integers); its lines (a
;; count, the integers); its positions (0 none, 1 then a string).
;; A constant is a tag (irC*) then its value; an argument and a tagged constant's value are generic values (irG*).

